  "sourceFindings": [
    "Current method2 prepares final decisions once, records coefficient statistics while coefficients are available, updates final probabilities, then final partition coding traverses levels again. tokenBuffer is a statistics-policy flag, not a retained token stream.",
    "Coefficients and statistics both derive last/band/context/category branches. Writer additionally emits fixed category/sign bits; statistics has distinct direct node9/node10 policy. Arithmetic writing remains necessary, so sample counts do not bound removable CPU.",
    "Skip probability is decided only after all blocks. All-zero skipped blocks must omit events and publish exact top/left resets, preserving Y2 through I4. Zero segment-header-cost policy leaves probabilities/default skip unchanged.",
    "Method0/1 statistics decisions are not final; rate-distortion methods use token-buffer counter policy and retries. Do not reuse first-pass decisions/events or apply method2 assumptions to those paths.",
    "Prediction still reconstructs identical borders/interpolation and source4row packing for ordered modes. Prepared prediction is an independent smaller lead; pruning may make eager all10 candidates wasteful."
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A materially revised compact coefficient-instruction program for finalmethod2 traversal: one instruction describes adaptive base, magnitude/category payload, sign and EOB scheduling, instead of one ushort per emitted arithmetic bit. Finalprobabilities remain indexed; preserve skip/context/direct-counterpolicy. First prove instruction grammar and bound/count representation against frozen current frame before production edits.",
  "intendedEndState": "One shared RFC6386 residual instruction construction during finalstatistics; replay resolves finalprobabilities and performs required arithmetic writing. Block coefficient scratch retires after reconstruction/statistics, admitted private instructionchunks remain until partition users finish. No permanent fullframe duplication, no pool/generalcache/session. Sparse/dense growth and replacement overlap charged before allocation.",
